Overlay patch 0045: stereoscopic eye rendering for visionOS 3D (reference
0031 ported; vision playbook §2.4/§2.5). The shell's CompositorServices loop
(SohImmersive.m) composites two per-eye Metal textures onto a world-locked
panel; this patch makes Fast3D produce them: in 3D mode (gSoh3DMode,
shell-owned), Fast3dWindow runs the interpreter TWICE per host frame — same
game time, same command list — with an eye state that (a) swaps mGameFb to a
per-eye framebuffer (all existing offscreen plumbing targets it
transparently) and (b) applies off-axis stereo to PERSPECTIVE projection
matrices only.

GHOSTSHIP DIVERGENCE — SIMPLER STEREO MATH THAN EVERY ZELDA PORT: SM64
submits perspective-ONLY through G_MTX_PROJECTION; the camera/lookat lives in
the MODELVIEW stack (geo_process_camera -> gMatStack). The matrix input space
at the injection sites is therefore VIEW space already, so the Ship of Harkinian port
hardest-won piece — the exported-camera-basis fold (their 0031 rev4 + 0032)
— is unnecessary: eye translation is row3 += -e*row0 and the convergence
shear is row2 += (-e/C)*row0, both derived from the matrix itself (row0
carries P00 and any screen-roll mixing). No basis/P00 exports; the game side
(0046) only writes gSoh3DCamDist + three comfort flags.

SKYBOX: SM64 draws its sky through an ORTHO pass (create_skybox_ortho_matrix)
— the perspective-detect would park it at ZERO disparity ON the panel,
stereoscopically in FRONT of the terrain behind it (the OoT "disorienting
clouds" bug, different mechanism). Between 0047's G_NOOP sentinels the ortho
matrix instead gets a constant clip-space shift equal to the perspective
background-disparity asymptote ((e/C)*lastP00) — sky at infinity.

Ports the Ship of Harkinian port device-proven machinery verbatim where the fork allows:
double-buffered eyes + completion-handler publish (the compositor blit-copies
UNFENCED from its own queue — commit-time publish loses the final ImGui pass
on device ONLY; sim serializes queues and hides it), no SetEye(0) per frame
(dims-flap resizes every game fb every frame = black-sky wedge), fb0 never
touched in 3D, both eyes every host frame (alternation judders), adaptive
convergence (sep proportional to smoothed camDist; clamp [50,6000] SM64
units, fallback 1000 — Lakitu orbits ~800-1400), pause/menu + aiming (C-up)
comfort blends.

Fork-B adaptations (vs reference 0031): no pending-mips flush (this fork's
0019 rev5 mips are CPU-side at upload), EndFrameOffscreen re-derived from
this fork's EndFrame (adds mLastStrictDecal reset; no readback/GPU-ms —
fb0-only concerns), Context::GetInstance (no GetRawInstance), 3-arg
Interpreter::Run (dlReplacements), post-pass chain gated OFF in eye passes
(would run twice into SHARED ping-pong fbs; publish ignores postOutputFb),
RunGuiOnly guarded (second fb0 path), stereo state also gates 0032's SSAA
rescale (see its rev2 comment). All new code is __IOS__-gated; shell globals
live in SohIosShell.m (iPhone links resolve; mode stays 0 there).

